  perform public.add_offseason_program('Off-Season – Cycling', 'For road Cycling: an 8-week off-season program. It builds leg and hip strength for more power on the pedals, a strong back and core so you can hold your position, a bigger aerobic base, and a sharper sprint. Each week has 2 strength sessions (Monday and Thursday, before your ride or on their own), 1 interval ride (Tuesday), 1 easy recovery ride with mobility (Wednesday), 1 sprint session (Friday) and a long easy ride on Saturday. Sunday is full rest. Strength in the off-season makes you stronger on the pedals and harder to injure without adding much bulk. Weeks 1-3 build (sets and ride time go up each week), week 4 is a recovery week at half the sets, weeks 5-7 add power and harder intervals, and week 8 is a test week at half the sets: test your best clean set on the squat and a 20-minute all-out effort, then you''re ready for the season. No set goes to failure: stop each set with 1-2 good reps left.',
    nutrition, warm_up, '{"1": "Strength A", "2": "Interval ride", "3": "Recovery ride + mobility", "4": "Strength B", "5": "Sprints & cadence", "6": "Long ride", "7": "Full rest"}'::jsonb,
